WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:19.468
Mary was so tired that she went to bed right after supper.

2
00:00:19.469 --> 00:00:24.068
In the middle of the night, she was awakened by dreadful sounds.

3
00:00:24.069 --> 00:00:28.273
Someone was crying and screaming at the same time.

4
00:00:28.274 --> 00:00:35.721
"It's Colin," she said. "He's having a tantrum. He sounds hysterical!"

5
00:00:35.722 --> 00:00:40.146
She suddenly understood why people always gave in to him.

6
00:00:40.147 --> 00:00:44.784
Anything was better than listening to these horrible, sobbing screams.

7
00:00:44.785 --> 00:00:50.294
She was terrified. But at the same time, she was angry.

8
00:00:50.295 --> 00:00:54.892
"Somebody ought to make him stop!" she cried.

9
00:00:54.893 --> 00:00:59.016
Just then she heard a person running down the corridor.

10
00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:02.579
Her door opened, and the nurse came in.

11
00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:07.848
"He's worked himself into hysterics," the nurse said breathlessly.

12
00:01:07.849 --> 00:01:13.301
"He'll do himself harm. No one can do anything with him.

13
00:01:13.302 --> 00:01:17.366
You must come and try to help him. He likes you."

14
00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:20.223
Mary flew down the corridor.

15
00:01:20.224 --> 00:01:24.733
The closer she got to Colin's room, the angrier she grew.

16
00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:28.667
She threw open the door and ran to Colin's bed.

17
00:01:28.668 --> 00:01:34.906
"Stop it!" she shouted at him. "Everybody hates you!

18
00:01:34.907 --> 00:01:39.795
I wish everybody would run away and let you scream yourself to death!"

19
00:01:39.796 --> 00:01:46.322
A nice, sympathetic child would never have thought such things, never mind said them.

20
00:01:46.323 --> 00:01:50.211
But it was the best possible thing for Colin to hear.

21
00:01:50.212 --> 00:01:54.614
He had been lying on his stomach, beating his pillow with his hands.

22
00:01:54.615 --> 00:02:00.330
But at the sound of Mary's furious voice, he turned around suddenly.

23
00:02:00.331 --> 00:02:06.058
His face was red and swollen from crying, and he was gasping and choking.

24
00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:08.550
Mary did not care.

25
00:02:08.551 --> 00:02:13.792
"If you scream another scream," she threatened, "I'll scream too.

26
00:02:13.793 --> 00:02:17.861
I can scream louder than you can, and I'll frighten you."

27
00:02:17.862 --> 00:02:26.567
"I can't stop!" Colin gasped. He was shaking all over. "I can't!"

28
00:02:26.568 --> 00:02:29.880
"You can!" shouted Mary.

29
00:02:29.881 --> 00:02:34.226
"Most of what's wrong with you is your temper and hysterics.

30
00:02:34.227 --> 00:02:37.947
Just hysterics, hysterics, hysterics!"

31
00:02:37.948 --> 00:02:42.360
She stamped her foot each time she said the word.

32
00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:50.443
"I felt a lump," choked out Colin. "I'll be a hunchback. I'm going to die."

33
00:02:50.444 --> 00:02:56.053
He turned on his stomach again and began to sob, but he didn't scream.

34
00:02:56.054 --> 00:03:02.134
"Nurse!" Mary commanded. "Come here and show me his back."

35
00:03:02.135 --> 00:03:09.393
The nurse, Mrs. Medlock, and Martha had been standing together near the door, watching her deal with Colin.

36
00:03:09.394 --> 00:03:13.321
More than once they had gasped with fright.

37
00:03:13.322 --> 00:03:17.711
"Perhaps he won't let me," said the nurse.

38
00:03:17.712 --> 00:03:23.332
"Show her!" said Colin. "Then she'll see."

39
00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:26.591
What a poor, thin back it was.

40
00:03:26.592 --> 00:03:31.666
Every rib could be counted and so could every bone of the spine.

41
00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:37.156
But Mary did not count them as she bent over his back and studied it solemnly.

42
00:03:37.157 --> 00:03:41.179
Everyone in the room waited breathlessly.

43
00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:45.584
"There's not a single lump there," Mary said at last.

44
00:03:45.585 --> 00:03:48.719
"The only lumps are backbone lumps.

45
00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:52.214
And you can only feel those because you're so thin.

46
00:03:52.215 --> 00:03:57.103
Mine used to stick out just as much as yours until I started getting fatter."

47
00:03:57.104 --> 00:04:02.607
"I didn't know that he thought he had a lump on his spine," said the nurse.

48
00:04:02.608 --> 00:04:07.040
"His back is weak because he refuses to sit up."

49
00:04:07.041 --> 00:04:09.901
Colin lay still for a minute.

50
00:04:09.902 --> 00:04:14.522
Huge tears streamed down his face and wet the pillow.

51
00:04:14.523 --> 00:04:20.374
He felt so relieved. Finally he spoke to the nurse again.

52
00:04:20.375 --> 00:04:23.462
"Do you think I could live to grow up?"

53
00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:29.201
"You probably could, if you do what you're told and go outside often."

54
00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:32.332
Colin's tantrum had left him weak.

55
00:04:32.333 --> 00:04:37.248
He put out his hand toward Mary, and she reached over and took it.

56
00:04:37.249 --> 00:04:42.582
"I'll go out with you, Mary. I won't hate fresh air if we can find . . ."

57
00:04:42.583 --> 00:04:47.207
He stopped himself just before saying the secret garden.

58
00:04:47.208 --> 00:04:51.384
"I'd like to go out if Dickon would come and push my wheelchair.

59
00:04:51.385 --> 00:04:56.502
I very much want to see him and the fox and crow."

60
00:04:56.503 --> 00:05:00.516
The nurse plumped up Colin's pillow and remade his bed.

61
00:05:00.517 --> 00:05:03.735
Then she brought tea to Colin and Mary.

62
00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:09.273
"He'll need to sleep soon," she said just before she left them alone.

63
00:05:09.274 --> 00:05:13.050
"Would you like me to sing to you?" asked Mary.

64
00:05:13.051 --> 00:05:16.818
"What I'd really like is to hear more about the secret garden.

65
00:05:16.819 --> 00:05:22.634
Did you notice I almost mentioned it? Have you found out any more about it?"

66
00:05:22.635 --> 00:05:26.198
Mary hesitated. "I think I have."

67
00:05:26.199 --> 00:05:30.240
"Oh, if I could go there, I think I could live to grow up.

68
00:05:30.241 --> 00:05:32.694
What do you think it looks like?"

69
00:05:32.695 --> 00:05:35.815
"Well . . ." Mary gulped.

70
00:05:35.816 --> 00:05:39.460
"I think everything has grown into a lovely tangle.

71
00:05:39.461 --> 00:05:44.379
There are probably lots of roses just starting to wake up.

72
00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:50.603
I think daffodils and snowdrops and lilies are working their way out of the ground.

73
00:05:50.604 --> 00:05:54.975
Maybe there are clusters of purple and gold crocuses."

74
00:05:54.976 --> 00:05:58.993
She looked over at Colin, who had fallen asleep.

75
00:05:58.994 --> 00:06:09.289
"And perhaps," she said softly, "perhaps the robin has found a mate and is building a nest."
